  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: 'Once a recipe only found in the diaspora enclaves
    in the eastern clusters of Verehn, the "long dough boil" as it is literally translated
    into Aijin tongue has been integrated into many dishes for all to enjoy in the
    gastronomy capital of the world. '
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: Verehn absorbed so many culinary traditions and
    techniques, it can make anybody feel bloated from the inside out. The hastily-made
    noodles contract and expand, releasing pitch-black oil at its ends. This "omentum"
    reportedly tastes like chicken, and is extracted for use in other recipes.
